 USSR were generally considered to be strong favorites despite having lost the world title at the 1959 World Championships, when Hungary had produced a shocking victory over a Soviet team that included the three fencers who swept the medals in the individual event. In Roma, the Soviets were desperately lucky to survive a quarter-final meeting with France, where they only won via the tie-break rule after winning the last five bouts in a row, but then easily defeated the Italian and Hungarian on their way to victory. Hungary placed second ahead of Italy."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitors"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} "Soviet Union"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/URS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/URS.png"}] "URS"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {:colspan "8"} [:a {:href "/athletes/20973"} "Valentina Rastvorova"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/20963"} "Galina Gorokhova"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/20969"} "Tatyana Petrenko"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/20976"} "Lyudmila Shishova"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/20972"} "Valentina Prudskova"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/20983"} "Aleksandra Zabelina"]]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} "Hungary"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/HUN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/HUN.png"}] "HUN"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {:colspan "8"} [:a {:href "/athletes/20753"} "Ildikó Rejtő"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/20756"} "Györgyi Marvalics-Székely"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/20751"} "Magda Nyári-Kovács"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/20741"} "Katalin Juhász"] " •